<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pa'O people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pa-O, Taungthu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pa'O are a Karen-speaking people of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a> of Myanmar, living mainly around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taunggyi">Taunggyi</a> and the hills near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inle-lake">Inle Lake</a>, and are one of the country's larger ethnic minorities. Traditionally Buddhist farmers known for growing thanaphet leaves for cheroots, they lived under Shan princes such as those of Yawnghwe and Mongnai. Since independence Pa'O groups have had their own armed organisations and a self-administered zone.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pao-people.jpg" alt="Pa'O people" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: exfordy · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pa-O_women_selling_vegetables,_Myanmar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
